d 'POLYREG': module to perform-regression on a polychoric index with bootstrap inference that accounts for the estimated index (generated-regressor correction)
d
d      Wealth or socioeconomic-status indices built by polychoric
d principal component analysis are routinely used as regressors.
d The	 usual practice computes the index once and then treats it
d as data. This ignores the sampling error in the index weights   
d (loadings and thresholds), so the reported standard errors are
d too small (the generated-regressor problem; Pagan 1984; Murphy   
d and Topel 1985).    polyreg builds the index with polyindex and
d fits the outcome model.  It then bootstraps the whole procedure,
d optionally by    cluster. In every replication, the polychoric
d correlations, thresholds and eigenvectors are re-estimated, the
d index is    recomputed (and, with quantiles(), regrouped), and
d the outcome model is re-fitted. The bootstrap covariance matrix
d of the    outcome-model coefficients is posted in e(V). For the
d index terms, the display compares bootstrap standard errors with
d the naive    (robust or cluster) standard errors and reports
d their ratio. 
d
d KW: polychoric index
d KW: bootstrap inference 
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author:  Yusuf Toyin Yusuf,  Kwara State University
d Support: email  YUSUF.YUSUF@@KWASU.EDU.NG
d
f polyreg.ado
f polyreg.sthlp
f polyreg_example.do
f polyreg_cert.do
